# Alembic migrations — MineralVision API

Run all commands from `MineralVision_Final_Package/` (where `alembic.ini` lives).

## Database URL resolution
1. `DATABASE_URL` env var (production: `postgresql+psycopg2://user:pass@host:5432/mineralvision`)
2. `sqlite:///./mineralvision.db` dev fallback (matches `src/api/database.py`)
3. Tests/tools may override programmatically via `Config.set_main_option("sqlalchemy.url", ...)`.

## Commands
```bash
# Apply all migrations
DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg2://user:pass@host:5432/mineralvision alembic upgrade head

# Roll back one revision / roll back everything
alembic downgrade -1
alembic downgrade base

# Current revision & history
alembic current
alembic history --verbose

# Generate a new revision after changing models in src/api/database.py
alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe change"
# ALWAYS review the generated file before committing.

# Emit SQL without connecting (offline mode, for DBAs)
alembic upgrade head --sql
```

Note: `src.api.database.init_db()` uses `Base.metadata.create_all`, which is a
no-op on migrated databases but bypasses revision tracking on fresh ones. For
migrated deployments prefer `alembic upgrade head` over `create_all`.
